+<p>At tensor degree k, write</p>
+<div class="equation-block"><math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mo form="prefix" stretchy="true">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo form="postfix" stretchy="true">]</mo></mrow><mi>/</mi><mrow><mo form="prefix" stretchy="true">(</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo form="postfix" stretchy="true">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width="2.0em"></mspace><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width="2.0em"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>deg</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width="2.0em"></mspace><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">
+E=\mathbb C[S]/(\chi),\qquad \chi=\chi_{h,k},\qquad q=\deg\chi&gt;0,
